 "spec": "HALDEN PARCEL CO.: DOMESTIC TARIFF (edition 10)\n\nAll prices are in cents. Apply the sections in order.\n\n\u00a71 Delivery times. Zone A: next working day. Zone B: two working days. Zone C: three to five working days.\n\n\u00a72 Weight. Weights are always rounded upward to a whole kilogram, never to the nearest; the minimum is 1 kg.\n\n\u00a73 Reclassification. A DOCUMENT whose rounded actual weight exceeds 1 kg is treated as a PARCEL for all purposes in this tariff.\n\n\u00a74 Chargeable weight. For a PARCEL, the chargeable weight is the greater of its actual weight and its volumetric weight, where volumetric weight = length x width x height in cm / 4000. Each is rounded up separately before the two are compared. A DOCUMENT is always charged on its actual weight only.\n\n\u00a75 Base price. Zone A: 530 for the first kg, then 150 per further kg; Zone B: 660 for the first kg, then 260 per further kg; Zone C: 800 for the first kg, then 280 per further kg.\n\n\u00a76 Heavy items. For each chargeable kg above 8 kg, the per-kg rate is increased by 80 cents. The first 8 kg are charged at the ordinary rates.\n\n\u00a77 Claims. Loss or damage must be reported within 14 days of the delivery date with photographs of the packaging.\n\n\u00a78 Surcharges. A weekend collection (Sat/Sun) adds 25% of the base price, rounded down; the percentage is never applied to other surcharges. Postcodes that BEGIN with GT or XL are remote: add a flat 400 cents after any percentage surcharge.\n\n\u00a79 Discounts. For GOLD accounts, 10% (rounded down) is deducted from the base price and percentage surcharges only. Flat fees such as the remote-area or oversize fee are charged in full. Zone A consignments are excluded from the GOLD discount.\n\n\u00a710 Cap. A DOCUMENT never costs more than 800 cents in total, after all surcharges and discounts.\n\n\u00a711 Prohibited items. Lithium batteries, aerosols and perishable goods are not accepted for carriage.",
